ting injection family of maximal size, up to permutations of [k] and [n]. This is not the case for small n. Indeed, we prove that if k is large in terms of k−t and n−k, the largest t-intersecting injection families are obtained from a process of saturation rather than fixing.\n\n\n## No full-text available\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nTo read the full-text of this research,\nyou can request a copy directly from the authors.\n\nRequest full-text PDF\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFor instance, we give the values of the coordinate statistics computed on the partition \\(\\pi=68-5-147-39-2\\): (https://dmtcs.episciences.org/en/articles/3508/download)\nciteturn1search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 20.1 years ago; Crawled: 6 days ago; For instance, we give the values of the coordinate statistics computed on the partition \\(\\pi=68-5-147-39-2\\): ... | \\(\\operatorname{lsb}_i\\) | 00 | 0 | 001 | 10 | 1 | ... Inspired by the statistic mak on the permutations due to Foata & Zeilberger [3], Steingrímsson introduced its analogous on \\(\\mathcal{OP}_n^k\\) as follows: ... The following proposition permits to reduce the conjecture 12 in [10] almost by half. ... The above theorem infers results on Euler-Mahonian statistics on ordered partitions.\n\nInspired by the statistic mak on the permutations due to Foata & Zeilberger [3], Steingrímsson introduced its analogous on \\(\\mathcal{OP}_n^k\\) as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\operatorname{mak}&=\\operatorname{ros}+\\operatorname{lcs},\\\\\n\\operatorname{lmak}&=n(k-1)-[\\operatorname{los}+\\operatorname{rcs}],\\\\\n\\operatorname{mak}'&=\\operatorname{lob}+\\operatorname{rcb},\\\\\n\\operatorname{lmak}'&=n(k-1)-[\\operatorname{lcb}+\\operatorname{rob}].\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nThe following proposition permits to reduce the conjecture 12 in [10] almost by half. This result was first proved in [4].\n\n**Proposition 1.8** On \\(\\mathcal{OP}_n^k\\) the following functional identities hold:\n\n\\[\n\\operatorname{mak}=\\operatorname{lmak}'\n\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n\\operatorname{mak}'=\\operatorname{lmak}.\n\\]\n\nDefine also the statistic \\(\\operatorname{cinvLSB}\\) on \\(\\mathcal{OP}^k\\) by\n\n\\[\n\\operatorname{cinvLSB}:=\\operatorname{lsb}+\\operatorname{cbInv}\n+\\binom{k}{2}.\n\\tag{5}\n\\]\n\n## 1.3 Main results\n\nConsider the following two generating functions of ordered partitions with \\(k\\geq 0\\) blocks:\n\n\\[\n\\phi_k(a;x,y,t,u):=\n\\sum_{\\pi\\in\\mathcal{OP}^k}\nx^{(\\operatorname{mak}+\\operatorname{bInv})\\pi}\ny^{\\operatorname{cinvLSB}\\pi}\nt^{\\operatorname{inv}\\pi}\nu^{\\operatorname{cinv}\\pi}\na^{|\\pi|},\n\\tag{6}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\varphi_k(a;z,t,u):=\n\\sum_{\\pi\\in\\mathcal{OP}^k}\nz^{(\\operatorname{lmak}+\\operatorname{bInv})\\pi}\nt^{\\operatorname{inv}\\pi}\nu^{\\operatorname{cinv}\\pi}\na^{|\\pi|},\n\\tag{7}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\(|\\pi|=n\\) if \\(\\pi\\) is a partition of \\([n]\\). The following Theorem is the main result of this paper.\n\n**Theorem 1.9** We have\n\n\\[\n\\phi_k(a;x,y,t,u)=\n\\frac{a^k(xy)^{\\binom{k}{2}}[k]_{tx,uy}!}\n{\\displaystyle\\prod_{i=1}^{k}(1-a[i]_{x,y})},\n\\tag{8}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\varphi_k(a;z,t,u)=\n\\frac{a^kz^{\\binom{k}{2}}[k]_{tz,u}!}\n{\\displaystyle\\prod_{i=1}^{k}(1-a[i]_z)}.\n\\tag{9}\n\\]\n\nThe above theorem infers results on Euler-Mahonian statistics on ordered partitions. Indeed, it follows directly from (2) that\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{n\\geq k}[k]_q!S_q(n,k)a^n\n=\n\\frac{a^kq^{\\binom{k}{2}}[k]_q!}\n{\\displaystyle\\prod_{i=1}^{k}(1-a[i]_q)}.\n\\tag{10}\n\\]\n\nThen, by appropriate specializations in (6) and (7), we obtain the following result conjectured by Steingrímsson [10, conj.12 and 13].--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nΑποτελέσματα αναζήτησης - \"Sophie Huczynska\" :: Library Catalog (https://vufind2.lib.aegean.gr/EDS/Search?dfApplied=1&filter%5B%5D=EXPAND%3A%22fulltext%22&filter%5B%5D=EXPAND%3